{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "moves.adjustments",
    "description": "Template library: the multiplicative adjustments applied to a zero-hour emission factor. `exhaust_temperature_adjustment` is docs/nonroad-logging-county.md §4.2 — an EXPONENTIAL of a piecewise-selected coefficient, exp((T <= 75 ? a_cold : a_hot) * (T - 75)), NOT the quadratic an earlier draft of PLAN.md called it; it is instantiated six ways (three pollutants x two gasoline stroke counts) and the 2-stroke instantiations carry both coefficients 0, so no branch is needed to switch it off. `oxygenate_adjustment` is §4.3, with the sign kept inside the coefficient exactly as exhaust.rs:606-625 keeps it (NOx uses c = -0.115, so `1 - c*oxy` grows), which is what lets one template serve all six instantiations. `exact_else_wildcard` is the two-step lookup precedence MOVES writes over and over — the exact key first, a designated wildcard row second, and the aggregate's own additive identity third: `BaseRateCalculator`'s temperature adjustment looks a row up by the exact regClassID and then by regClassID 0 (`baseratecalculator/adjust.rs:495-520`), and reaching the second step is what makes the EV temperature factor 1.015625 rather than 1 at 59.5 °F. Both arms are separate aggregates over the same table with different key pairs, and this template is the precedence between their results — so a document that computes only the exact arm reads as obviously incomplete beside one that instantiates this. `im_blend` is the onroad inspection/maintenance blend PLAN.md §3 names; it is not exercised by the NONROAD slice but is the same shape and belongs beside the others.\n\nTHE ONROAD RUNNING-EXHAUST ADJUSTMENTS `baseratecalculator/adjust.rs` applies in order, added when `process-nox-speciation` became the first fixture to compute a criteria pollutant rather than an energy or particulate one. `gpa_blend` is the two-arm fuel-effect blend the general-fuel-ratio and criteria-ratio steps BOTH perform (adjust.rs:465, :486) -- `ratio + gpaFract x (ratioGPA - ratio)` -- and it is one template because writing it twice is how the two arms come to disagree about which is the base. In a county whose `GPAFract` is 0 it selects the normal arm, which is every county in this repository's snapshots and is exactly why the blend has to be written rather than assumed. `quadratic_temperature_adjustment` is `general_temp_adjust`'s last line (adjust.rs:142), the fall-through every pollutant with no special branch takes, centred on `exhaust_temperature_reference` so the 75 exists once. `nox_temperature_adjustment` is the NOx branch above it (adjust.rs:127-139), and its asymmetry is the point: DIESEL is `(77 - T) x A` and is switched OFF above 77 degF, every other fuel is the ordinary centred quadratic about 75 -- two different reference temperatures in one branch, which is not a thing a reader guesses. `nox_humidity_cfr86` and `nox_humidity_cfr1065` are `calculate_nox_k` (adjust.rs:168-188): the humidity correction MOVES multiplies the NOx temperature factor by, selected by a TEXT column (`noxhumidityadjust.humidityNOxEq`), linear in bounded specific humidity for CFR 86 and reciprocal in bounded water mole fraction for CFR 1065. `bounded_low_then_high` is that pair's `bound_humidity`, and it is the Go's two sequential assignments rather than a clamp: `min(max(v, lo), up)` agrees with them everywhere including `lo > up`, where both yield `up` and a three-argument clamp would panic. A fuel type with no `noxhumidityadjust` row takes no correction at all, which is the caller's `map_or(1.0, ...)` and not a template's business.\n\n`speciation_factor` is `HCSpeciationCalculator`'s NMOG/VOC multiplier (hcspeciation.rs:616-617): `speciationConstant + oxySpeciation x volToWtPercentOxy x totalOxygenate`, where `totalOxygenate` is the fuel formulation's MTBE + ETBE + TAME + ETOH volume. It is one template rather than two because NMOG and VOC take the SAME form from the SAME table under different `polProcessID`s, and written twice the two could disagree about which of the three factors the oxygenate volume multiplies. Instantiated four times by fixtures/process-airtoxics.esm -- VOC on the emission's own fuel subtype and VOC on the E10 subtype of the altTHC path, each in its value and its existence arm.\n\nTHE PM ARM AND THE FUEL-SULFUR SULFATE ADJUSTMENT, added when `process-pm-exhaust` became the first fixture whose pollutants are exhaust PARTICULATE. `pm_temperature_adjustment` is `general_temp_adjust`'s FIRST branch (adjust.rs:105-110), the one every earlier onroad rung fell past: for pollutant 118 or 112 on process 1 or 2 the temperature factor is MULTIPLICATIVE and exponential, exp(A x (72 - least(T, 72))), not the additive quadratic `quadratic_temperature_adjustment` carries -- and docs/process-airtoxics.md 2.2 says so from the other side, that pollutant 1 takes the fall-through arm precisely because it is not 118/112. The Rust writes the ceiling as a BRANCH (`if temperature <= 72.0 { exp(...) } else { 1.0 }`) and this writes it as `least(T, 72)` inside the exponent, which is the same function -- exp(0) is 1 -- and is how `start_temp_adjust` in that same file spells the identical ceiling three screens above. One expression rather than a branch means `pm_temperature_ceiling` exists once; it is a separate zero-parameter template for the same reason `exhaust_temperature_reference` and `nox_diesel_temperature_ceiling` are, so that a document instantiating this carries no bare 72 (docs/esm-conventions.md 24). There is no B term in this arm, and `process-pm-exhaust` therefore computes no B column at all.\n\n`fuel_sulfur_sulfate_adjustment` is `SulfatePMCalculator`'s `oneCountyYearSulfateFractions` extract (sulfate_pm_calculator.rs:838-841): 1 + BaseFuelSulfateFraction x (sulfurLevel / BaseFuelSulfurLevel - 1), the factor by which a supplied formulation's own sulfur moves the tabulated sulfate share of composite non-EC particulate. It is ONE template because it multiplies the sulfate fraction and the water fraction both, and written twice the two could disagree about which end the -1 belongs to -- the same argument that makes `gpa_blend` and `speciation_factor` one template each. Two cautions for a caller. The divisor is a table value that is 0 where the lookup MISSED, and 0/0 is NaN which no multiplicative gate can suppress, so the caller substitutes a VALUE for it (fixtures/process-pm-exhaust.esm's `rt_baseFuelSulfurLevelGuarded`; docs/esm-conventions.md 29). And the adjusted fraction is not the whole story: MOVES splits the residue with the UNADJUSTED fractions, so the three species do not sum to the parent they came from, and that asymmetry belongs to the caller rather than to this template.",
    "authors": ["EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"],
    "tags": ["moves", "nonroad", "onroad", "adjustments", "template-library"]
  },
  "expression_templates": {
    "exhaust_temperature_reference": {
      "params": [],
      "body": 75.0
    },
    "exhaust_temperature_adjustment": {
      "params": ["a_cold", "a_hot", "temperature"],
      "body": {
        "op": "exp",
        "args": [
          {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "ifelse",
                "args": [
                  { "op": "<=", "args": ["temperature",
                    { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "exhaust_temperature_reference", "bindings": {} }] },
                  "a_cold",
                  "a_hot"
                ]
              },
              { "op": "-", "args": ["temperature",
                { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "exhaust_temperature_reference", "bindings": {} }] }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    "oxygenate_adjustment": {
      "params": ["coefficient", "oxygen_weight_percent"],
      "body": {
        "op": "-",
        "args": [1.0, { "op": "*", "args": ["coefficient", "oxygen_weight_percent"] }]
      }
    },
    "exact_else_wildcard": {
      "params": ["has_exact", "exact_value", "wildcard_value"],
      "body": {
        "op": "ifelse",
        "args": [
          { "op": ">", "args": ["has_exact", 0.5] },
          "exact_value",
          "wildcard_value"
        ]
      }
    },
    "gpa_blend": {
      "params": ["ratio", "ratio_gpa", "gpa_fraction"],
      "body": {
        "op": "+",
        "args": ["ratio",
          { "op": "*", "args": ["gpa_fraction",
            { "op": "-", "args": ["ratio_gpa", "ratio"] }] }]
      }
    },
    "bounded_low_then_high": {
      "params": ["value", "low_bound", "up_bound"],
      "body": {
        "op": "min",
        "args": [
          { "op": "max", "args": ["value", "low_bound"] },
          "up_bound"
        ]
      }
    },
    "nox_humidity_reference": {
      "params": [],
      "body": 10.71
    },
    "nox_humidity_cfr86": {
      "params": ["term_a", "bounded_specific_humidity"],
      "body": {
        "op": "-",
        "args": [1.0,
          { "op": "*", "args": ["term_a",
            { "op": "-", "args": ["bounded_specific_humidity",
              { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "nox_humidity_reference", "bindings": {} }] }] }]
      }
    },
    "nox_humidity_cfr1065": {
      "params": ["term_a", "term_b", "bounded_mole_fraction"],
      "body": {
        "op": "/",
        "args": [1.0,
          { "op": "+", "args": [
            { "op": "*", "args": ["term_a", "bounded_mole_fraction"] },
            "term_b"] }]
      }
    },
    "nox_diesel_temperature_ceiling": {
      "params": [],
      "body": 77.0
    },
    "quadratic_temperature_adjustment": {
      "params": ["term_a", "term_b", "temperature"],
      "body": {
        "op": "*",
        "args": [
          { "op": "-", "args": ["temperature",
            { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "exhaust_temperature_reference", "bindings": {} }] },
          { "op": "+", "args": ["term_a",
            { "op": "*", "args": ["term_b",
              { "op": "-", "args": ["temperature",
                { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "exhaust_temperature_reference", "bindings": {} }] }] }] }]
      }
    },
    "nox_temperature_adjustment": {
      "params": ["term_a", "term_b", "temperature", "is_diesel"],
      "body": {
        "op": "ifelse",
        "args": [
          { "op": ">", "args": ["is_diesel", 0.5] },
          {
            "op": "ifelse",
            "args": [
              { "op": ">", "args": ["temperature",
                { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "nox_diesel_temperature_ceiling", "bindings": {} }] },
              0.0,
              { "op": "*", "args": [
                { "op": "-", "args": [
                  { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "nox_diesel_temperature_ceiling", "bindings": {} },
                  "temperature"] },
                "term_a"] }
            ]
          },
          { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "quadratic_temperature_adjustment",
            "bindings": { "term_a": "term_a", "term_b": "term_b", "temperature": "temperature" } }
        ]
      }
    },
    "im_blend": {
      "params": ["rate_im", "fraction_im", "rate_base"],
      "body": {
        "op": "max",
        "args": [
          {
            "op": "+",
            "args": [
              { "op": "*", "args": ["rate_im", "fraction_im"] },
              { "op": "*", "args": ["rate_base", { "op": "-", "args": [1.0, "fraction_im"] }] }
            ]
          },
          0.0
        ]
      }
    },
    "pm_temperature_ceiling": {
      "params": [],
      "body": 72.0
    },
    "pm_temperature_adjustment": {
      "params": ["term_a", "temperature"],
      "body": {
        "op": "exp",
        "args": [
          { "op": "*", "args": [
            "term_a",
            { "op": "-", "args": [
              { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "pm_temperature_ceiling", "bindings": {} },
              { "op": "min", "args": [
                "temperature",
                { "op": "apply_expression_template", "args": [], "name": "pm_temperature_ceiling", "bindings": {} }
              ] }
            ] }
          ] }
        ]
      }
    },
    "fuel_sulfur_sulfate_adjustment": {
      "params": ["base_fuel_sulfate_fraction", "sulfur_level", "base_fuel_sulfur_level"],
      "body": {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
          1.0,
          { "op": "*", "args": [
            "base_fuel_sulfate_fraction",
            { "op": "-", "args": [
              { "op": "/", "args": ["sulfur_level", "base_fuel_sulfur_level"] },
              1.0
            ] }
          ] }
        ]
      }
    },
    "speciation_factor": {
      "params": ["speciation_constant", "oxy_speciation", "vol_to_wt_percent_oxy", "total_oxygenate"],
      "body": {
        "op": "+",
        "args": [
          "speciation_constant",
          { "op": "*", "args": [
            "oxy_speciation",
            { "op": "*", "args": ["vol_to_wt_percent_oxy", "total_oxygenate"] }
          ] }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
